## Brand and writing source decisions

The [brand inventory](../reference/brand-guidance.json) maps the four requested Brand sections and their linked guidance to local rules. The official graphic device, logo system and brand-in-use sections are excluded from this work package.

The [writing inventory](../reference/writing-guide.json) records the reviewed chapters, local rules, exclusions and source conflicts for:

- [NHS content guidance](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/content): user needs, plain language, interface content and inclusion.
- [Home Office content style guide](https://design.homeoffice.gov.uk/design-and-content/content/content-style-guide): consistent terminology and accessible public-facing content.
- [GOV.UK publishing writing guidelines](https://guidance.publishing.service.gov.uk/writing-to-gov-uk-standards/writing-guidelines/): clear language, structure, tone and editorial work.
- [Plain English Campaign free guides](https://www.plainenglish.co.uk/free-guides): clear explanations, forms, layout and proofreading. The four reviewed guide titles are recorded in the inventory; the PDFs remain with their publisher.
- [SCULPT](https://www.worcestershire.gov.uk/council-services/business/digital-worcestershire/sculpt-accessibility/what-sculpt): an accessibility review prompt developed by Helen Wilson at Worcestershire County Council.

These sources inform original household rules and examples. Civica does not copy their organisational workflows or claim endorsement. The [writing guide](../content/index.html) explains how to resolve conflicting advice; [licensing](licensing.html) records the separate source-material terms.

## Component and pattern sources

Component guidance is adapted from the [GOV.UK Design System](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/) and the [NHS digital service manual](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system). Specific sources are [NHS hint text](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/hint-text), [NHS buttons](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/buttons) and [GOV.UK warning text](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/warning-text/). Navigation, modal and card references draw on the [Ministry of Justice design system](https://design-patterns.service.justice.gov.uk/), and chart and data presentation on the [Office for National Statistics design system](https://service-manual.ons.gov.uk/design-system). The examples use shared GOV.UK primitives or original Civica markup.

Pattern guidance is adapted from the [NHS digital service manual](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system), the [GOV.UK Design System](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/), the [GOV.UK Brand guidelines](https://brand.design-system.service.gov.uk/) and the [Office for National Statistics design system](https://service-manual.ons.gov.uk/design-system). Specific sources:

- NHS patterns: [question pages](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/question-pages), [know that a page is up to date](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/know-that-a-page-is-up-to-date), [ask for NHS numbers](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/ask-for-nhs-numbers), [start page](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/start-page), [find BSL content](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/find-bsl-content), [A to Z page](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/a-to-z-page), [check answers](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/check-answers), [complete multiple tasks](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/complete-multiple-tasks), [confirmation page](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/confirmation-page), [hub page](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/hub-page), [mini hub](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/mini-hub), [interruption page](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/interruption-page) and [help users decide when and where to get care](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/patterns/help-users-decide-when-and-where-to-get-care).
- NHS components: [cards](https://service-manual.nhs.uk/design-system/components/card).
- GOV.UK Design System: [error message](https://design-system.service.gov.uk/components/error-message/). GOV.UK Brand guidelines: [dashboards](https://brand.design-system.service.gov.uk/data/dashboards/).
- ONS design system: column chart, stacked bar chart and line chart guidance, and dashboard guidance.

Civica is an independent project. It is not endorsed by these organisations, and NHS logos and service identity are not used. [Licensing and attribution](licensing.html) gives the licence terms and notices.

